{
  "format": "rustsheet-case/v1",
  "description": "T-4228: which group Excel puts a value in for pivot fields grouped by numeric ranges (<rangePr>), and GETPIVOTDATA on a group label. Each record's S value is a distinct power of two, so a group's sum names its records. Pivot 1 (P) groups N1 by 0.1 from 0 to 1 with a ladder of values just below 0.3 and 1, pivot 2 (Q) by 0.1 from 1 to 2, pivot 3 (R) by 3 from 0 to 9 with one group item too many (Excel relabels it), pivot 4 (S) the same with Excel's own labels, pivot 5 (T) by 0.001 from 0 to 1 with a ladder just below 0.123. Calc reads GETPIVOTDATA per label and the cells Excel renders (rows 3 on, as text); A30:A41 are further GETPIVOTDATA forms on pivot 1 and C30:C47 numbers as items.",
